@prefix chorus: <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# =============================================================================
# #4045 — the 18 served Documents, in a file, so a product seed can resolve its
# hasDesignDoc edge in a store that starts empty (the werk store at env-up).
#
# The products batch refused on 2026-09-02 09:47 for a missing comment, and
# would have refused next on hasDesignDoc: the seeder's referential-integrity
# check is fail-closed against the store OR the batch (#3839), and no Document
# existed in the werk store. Same pattern as roles (#3838): live-only until
# authored. Exported from urn:chorus:domains:documents 2026-09-02 09:55.
#
# NOTE: seed --deploy loads the whole manifest into urn:chorus:instances (one
# batch, one graph), while DocumentShape pins urn:chorus:domains:documents and
# /documents serves from there. In prod the rows already exist in the pinned
# graph, so this adds a second copy in instances (the two spine docs already had
# one); in the werk store it is what lets Product rows resolve. Per-group graph
# pins in seed --deploy are the clean close — noted on #4062 (/ca).
# =============================================================================

# #4045 — was chorus:doc-product-design-pulse (outside the ADR-040 document- convention; the seeder's iri-guard refused it). Renamed; prod keeps the old row in urn:chorus:domains:documents until retired.
chorus:document-product-design-pulse a chorus:Document ;
    chorus:docState """current""" ;
    chorus:docTitle """Product Design — Pulse""" ;
    chorus:docHref """/designing/docs/product-design-pulse.html""" ;
    chorus:comment """What Pulse is FOR: Jeff looks once and knows whether his team is working, without asking anyone and without being lied to. Measured by how many times a day he has to ask — six on 2026-08-25.""" ;
    rdfs:comment """What Pulse is FOR: Jeff looks once and knows whether his team is working, without asking anyone and without being lied to. Measured by how many times a day he has to ask — six on 2026-08-25.""" ;
    chorus:hasDomain chorus:memory ;
    chorus:ownedBy chorus:role-wren ;
    chorus:hasProduct chorus:pulse .

